Description: Install the SIGTERM handler once the app shell exists, so that SIGTERM quits Firefox cleanly.
 Bug 1837907 added a handler which quits Firefox cleanly on SIGTERM, saving its session, and calls
 nsAppShell::InstallTermSignalHandler() at the end of XREMain::XRE_mainStartup(). XPCOM, which creates the app shell,
 starts only after that function, so the handler finds no app shell and returns without installing anything. SIGTERM
 therefore kills Firefox at once, without saving its session, and the next start recovers from a crash. At the end of
 a desktop session systemd stops the applications still running with SIGTERM, so every logout and shutdown in which
 Firefox was still running counted as a crash.
 .
 The handler is now installed in XREMain::XRE_mainRun(), once XPCOM created the app shell, and still not in background
 task mode.
Bug: https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2086801
Author: Mitar
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-07
---
diff --git a/toolkit/xre/nsAppRunner.cpp b/toolkit/xre/nsAppRunner.cpp
index 513d100..e9a9cde 100644
--- a/toolkit/xre/nsAppRunner.cpp
+++ b/toolkit/xre/nsAppRunner.cpp
@@ -5966,9 +5966,6 @@ int XREMain::XRE_mainStartup(bool* aExitFlag) {
     if (IsWaylandEnabled()) {
       (void)WaylandDisplayGet();
     }
-#endif
-#ifdef MOZ_WIDGET_GTK
-    nsAppShell::InstallTermSignalHandler();
 #endif
   }
 
@@ -6387,6 +6384,14 @@ nsresult XREMain::XRE_mainRun() {
         g_unsetenv(name.get());
       }
       nsAppShell::InitSessionRestore();
+#  ifdef MOZ_BACKGROUNDTASKS
+      if (!BackgroundTasks::IsBackgroundTaskMode())
+#  endif
+      {
+        // The app shell handles the signal, and XPCOM creates it only after
+        // XRE_mainStartup().
+        nsAppShell::InstallTermSignalHandler();
+      }
 #endif
 
 #ifdef XP_MACOSX
